      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing you could do is send as many consecutive iovs as you can as long as their total size does not exceed `MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE`.\n\nYou can implement that by maintaining a first-last contiguous iov range. Once the next iov causes the current range to go over, you send out the current range then update `first` to the current iov. If that one is larger than 4096 by itself, then you can break it up.\n\nYou _could_ also keep track of positions inside them and coalesce partial iovs, but that would make the implementation even more complex.",
      "revId": "d0f104d306db9e440fd2b1eda653c3344c390e27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
